 "text": "Okay, let's get started. This is the weekly sync for the payments platform. Arjun, Mira, thanks for joining. We have three things today: the latency issue, the caching plan, and the release on the 24th. Sure, so the P99 latency on the checkout API went up to 420 milliseconds last week. Most of it is coming from repeated post-gur SQL queries for the merchant config. Yes, I saw that in Grafana too. The P50 is fine, it's only the tail. Okay, Arjun, you had a proposal for caching. Right, I want to put Ridis in front of the Merchant Config table with a 5 minute TTL, in staging that brought the P99 down to 180 milliseconds. Five minutes is fine for config data, I'm okay with that. Great then let's go with riddies for the merchant config cache that's decided There was also the idea of moving the event pipeline to Kafka. I'd honestly like to do that, but not this quarter. We don't have the bandwidth. Agreed, we are not migrating to Kafka this quarter. Let's revisit it in January. Now, action items. Arjun, can you ship the Riddy's cash behind a feature flag by Thursday? Yes, I'll have it behind a flag by Thursday. And I'll write the rollback runbook for the cash Thanks. We also need to update the on-call rotation before the release. Yeah, someone should do that. And maybe Rohan could look into the flaky integration tests, but I'll have to ask him first. 1 open question: do we have budget for the extra GPU nodes for the fraud model? It's around $2,500 a month. I don't know yet, I'll check with finance, and get back to you by Monday One more thing. The Oauth token refresh bug is not blocking the release, so I'd keep it in the backlog. Fine, it stays in the backlog. Okay, the release is still on the 24th. Thanks, everyone. Thanks for watching!",
